{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q2235148","formula":"Na(Fe₃)Al₆(Si₆O₁₈)(BO₃)₃O₃F","hill":"Al6B3FFe3NaO30Si6","elements":["B","O","F","Na","Al","Si","Fe"],"composition":{"B":3.0,"F":1.0,"O":30.0,"Al":6.0,"Fe":3.0,"Na":1.0,"Si":6.0},"names":{"en":"Fluor-buergerite","uk":"Флюоро-бюргерит"},"descriptions":{"en":"Fluor-buergerite, originally named buergerite, is a mineral species belonging to the tourmaline group. It was first described for an occurrence in rhyolitic cavities near Mexquitic, San Luis Potosi, Mexico. It was approved as a mineral in 1966 by the IMA and named in honor of Martin J. Buerger (1903–1986), professor of mineralogy at the Massachusetts Institute of Technology.","uk":"Флюоро-бюргерит, спочатку названий у 1966 році бюргеритом, — мінерал, що належить до групи турмалінів. Вперше мінерал було описано за проявами у ліпаритових порожнинах поблизу Мескітіка, Сан-Луїс-Потосі, Мексика. Він був схвалений як мінерал у 1966 році IMA (Rd 1965—005) та названий на честь Мартіна Дж."},"fame":11,"pubchemCid":null,"mass":null,"charge":0,"smiles":null,"inchikey":null,"iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q12089225","names":{"en":"mineral species","ru":"действительный вид минералов","uk":"мінеральний вид"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"crystal","source":"materialsproject","ref":"mp-18401","atoms":164,"license":"CC BY 4.0, Materials Project"},"structure":{"cell":[[16.023,0.0,0.0],[-8.011,13.876,0.0],[0.0,0.0,7.318]],"kind":"crystal","atoms":[{"x":0.0,"y":0.0,"z":5.72,"el":"Na"},{"x":-8.011,"y":13.876,"z":5.72,"el":"Na"},{"x":16.023,"y":0.0,"z":5.72,"el":"Na"},{"x":8.011,"y":13.876,"z":5.72,"el":"Na"},{"x":3.535,"y":4.057,"z":5.333,"el":"Al"},{"x":2.73,"y":5.658,"z":0.454,"el":"Al"},{"x":-3.535,"y":13.308,"z":2.893,"el":"Al"},{"x":5.281,"y":1.033,"z":5.333,"el":"Al"},{"x":1.746,"y":4.161,"z":2.893,"el":"Al"},{"x":-1.746,"y":13.412,"z":0.454,"el":"Al"},{"x":6.363,"y":3.674,"z":5.238,"el":"Fe"},{"x":0.0,"y":1.903,"z":2.798,"el":"Fe"},{"x":-6.363,"y":12.925,"z":2.798,"el":"Fe"},{